{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792695466,"nonce":"ptIkjyC80/dKpKIHuXYlF8o+NB4=","title":"Native primitive stream drops path clips on SDF shapes, meshes and canvas text","message":"Scoped child of 732c3370857424d2e3c7ccfcde44fe0095471eda74dae4e5b415daca036738fe. Native GpuPaintContext primitive emission leaves clip_shape unset when the selected clip is a Path. This includes SDF shapes, tessellated solid/gradient fills and strokes routed through PRIM_MESH, shadows, and canvas text converted to PRIM_TEXT. The existing SDF shader variants already evaluate the ABI shape header and contour rows.\n\nAdd independent offscreen controls before connecting the push-time affine/fill-rule path preparation to that existing header. Preserve rectangular scissors, active batch ownership, foreground projection, drains, merges, canvas concatenation, scratch ancestor stripping and tight target translation. Cache path rows per owning batch rather than duplicating them per primitive/triangle/glyph. Keep checks scoped to touched files and relevant tests with CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2.\n\nSeparate native tessellated-path brush fallback, glass/backdrop clipping and independently prepared glyph/text streams remain on the parent. No shared ClipPath/CSS enum changes, arbitrary stacked-shape intersections, 3D mesh clipping, device performance claim or push is authorized by this slice.","files":null}]}